5. WIRE FORMAT COMPLIANCE — PASS
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Confirmed against the REAL endpoint, not just the code.

- delete_source deletes on the literal "true" and nothing else.
  handlers.go:586 is `r.PostFormValue("delete_source") == "true"` — a literal
  string comparison, not strconv.ParseBool. Live probe C sent
  `name=gamma.csv&delete_source=TRUE`: HTTP 200, "— imported" with no deletion
  reason, and `gamma src exists: YES`. Live probe B sent the literal `true`
  and gamma's sibling beta.csv was deleted. Test coverage:
  TestHandleImport_DeleteSourceOnlyOnLiteralTrue (handlers_test.go:2391)
  table-drives "1", "yes", "TRUE", "on", "" and asserts the source survives
  each.

- A name containing a path separator is rejected WITHOUT touching the
  filesystem. Static: the check at handlers.go:621-624 precedes every
  filesystem call in the function (the first is os.Lstat at 641). Live probe E
  `name=../outside/outside.csv&delete_source=true` -> HTTP 200 with body
  "../outside/outside.csv — rejected (invalid filename)";
  `outside survives: YES | leaked to data: NO`. I also probed a form the
  oracle does not cover, `name=subdir/nested.csv&delete_source=true` (probe G)
  -> "rejected (invalid filename)", `nested survives: YES`.
  Also verified the symlink arm (probe H): `name=link.csv&delete_source=true`
  -> "rejected (symlinks are not imported)", symlink target survives.

- 400 on no `name` fields, and that 400 is inert. handlers.go:581-584 returns
  before `deps := defaultImportDeps()` at 588 and before the per-file loop, so
  inertness is structural. Live probe I sent `delete_source=true` with no name
  field:
      HTTP 400, body "No files selected for import"
      import dir before: alpha.csv collide.csv delta.csv gamma.csv keepme.csv link.csv notes.txt subdir
      import dir after : alpha.csv collide.csv delta.csv gamma.csv keepme.csv link.csv notes.txt subdir
      INERT: YES
  Names are read from r.PostForm (handlers.go:575-576), not r.Form, so URL
  query parameters cannot smuggle in a selection — a detail the spec implies
  ("the selection belongs in the request body") and the code comments call
  out. Whitespace-only names are filtered at 577, covered by
  TestHandleImport_BlankNameIs400 (handlers_test.go:2707).

- 200 for a processed batch even with per-file skips: live probes D, F and J
  all returned HTTP 200 while reporting skipped/rejected outcomes in the body.

The form markup produces exactly this wire format: filemanager.html:1434 emits
`<input type="checkbox" name="name" value="{{$e.Name}}">` per entry and
filemanager.html:88 emits `name="delete_source" value="true"`, inside the
`<form hx-post="/explorer/import">` at line 80-81. Entries already in the data
dir render `disabled` (line 1435), and disabled inputs are not submitted.

